# Tracer: the function body comes from a forall premise, not a have fn declaration.
# The original internal name fn_definition_subterms obscured this existing source.
# FnApplicationUnfoldSubstitution reads the exact local f=AnonymousFn equality.
forall f fn(t R: t > 0) R, x R:
    f = fn(t R: t > 0) R {t}
    x > 0
    =>:
        2 * f(x) = 2 * x

# Boundary: function membership alone supplies no body; x>0 is still required.
# f(x)=f(x) would prove only reflexivity, so this tracer checks a body-dependent goal.
